\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Enriched backgrounds and comparison}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{A change of background must specify which structures it preserves.
The prerequisites are the [reference pairing](fdip-001N),
[split maps](fdip-001T) and [retained Gaussian law](fdip-000E).
A finite background first fixes these data; an
[intrinsic trace](fdip-003G) then defines a
[ratio on its unit-denominator domain](fdip-003H), which
[separates two weighted cycles](fdip-000I).}

\p{The [enriched groupoid](fdip-000X) records allowed arrows and
the data they preserve. [Scalar invariants](fdip-000Y) descend
along those arrows without classifying all backgrounds.
[Quadratic isometry](fdip-000Z) can forget the reference pairing or
retained projection even while transporting a positive Gaussian law.}

\transclude{fdip-000G}
